    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offensive output today hinges on **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who represents our strongest play with a 73.66 efficiency score. Facing Feltner, who carries a shaky 4.98 xERA, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a massive 19% boost in SP skill projection and a 14% platoon edge, effectively weaponizing his spot in the four-hole to anchor our run production. Following him is **Drake Baldwin**, our leadoff catcher, whose 68.36 score is buoyed by a favorable matchup against Martinez and a 10% bump for his premier batting order slot. While **Sam Antonacci** and **Dominic Smith** provide respectable mid-range stability, the reliance on **Drake Baldwin** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** to exploit these specific pitching matchups is paramount to keeping our 5x5 metrics\u2014specifically AVG and RBI\u2014on track for the week.\n\nThe bench remains a site of frustration today, as we are forced to sit our elite core\u2014**Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**\u2014due to league-wide off-days, while **Luis Robert Jr.** remains sidelined on the IL. With so many high-impact bats unavailable, **Miguel Vargas** earns the 1B start despite a mediocre 45.90 score; he barely held off internal depth options because his 0.383 xwOBA suggests he is better equipped to handle Jones than his raw projections imply. We are keeping a close watch on **Miguel Vargas** and **Sam Antonacci** against Jones\u2019s 3.57 xERA; though Jones is a tougher assignment than the pitchers facing our other starters, their lineup order helps mitigate the risk. Our focus remains on preserving game caps while looking toward the return of **Jackson Merrill**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jordan Westburg** to bolster the roster once the off-day congestion clears.",
